WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.380
Panda's Diet

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.080
Welcome.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.130
What's wrong? You look down.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.370
Do you want your usual, Panda?

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.710
Yes... Oh, but just 
a normal serving.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.030
What? You don't want 
the larger serving?

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.050
I'm starting a diet today.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.730
Diet <i>(daietto)</i>?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.880
That would be the Internet <i>(inta-netto)</i>.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.970
That would be Inuit <i>(inuitto)</i>.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.450
That would be a quartet <i>(karutetto)</i>.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.070
What brought this on?

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.950
Well you see, at the zoo today...

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.040
Mr. Panda!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.830
Service, service.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.130
I'm glad you weren't hurt.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.710
So you're starting a 
diet because of that?

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:54.960
Well, I always wished I was 
born a bit more slim.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.030
You care about your figure?

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.690
Yeah, considering I've had

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.840
the physique of an old man
 since I was born.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.910
Well, what do you want to look like?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.120
My ideal is...

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.540
For my legs to be longer,

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.400
an upside down triangle-shaped torso,

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.760
and for my face to be shaped like 
an inverted triangle, too.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.410
<i>Dream Panda!</i>

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.450
Is that actually cool?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.320
You'd look like a bad guy, Panda.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.420
That's fine.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.760
I think bad guys are awesome.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.670
Here you go.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.910
Here's the normal serving.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.420
Could I get my usual after all?

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:56.210
One large serving coming right up.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.030
What about your diet?

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.920
I'll start tomorrow.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:07.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.410
Mr. Panda!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.240
<i>Adrian!</i>

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.190
Wake up, Panda!

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.540
You only have to work twice a week,

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:56.290
so could you not sleep 
as soon as you get here?

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.730
Here you go, panda dumplings.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:01.990
I don't want them.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.840
What? Why?

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.920
I'm starting my diet today.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:08.200
Diet?

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:15.000
Wow, I'm definitely overweight, 
but I'm not doing a thing.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:21.010
Well, I broke the slide yesterday.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.480
Oh, I'm sorry about that.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.790
The supports were eaten away by termites,

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.760
It's wasn't your fault, Panda.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:33.060
Not to mention, I'm young and have 
the physique of an old man.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.350
Well, that's natural for a panda.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.020
Don't you know where the 
name "panda" comes from?

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.840
Ooh, what is it?

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.730
Does it come from "cute"?

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:48.300
Well, there are multiple explanations.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.450
One of them goes like this...

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:58.420
Long, long ago, there were 
foreigners exploring China.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.840
Oh, the fat one.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:18.310
So that's the explanation 
of the Chinese phrase for

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.600
"the fat one" becoming 
the name for panda.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.570
Then that would mean...

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:28.580
Panda! Panda!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.040
Overweight! Overweight!

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.450
I'm starting to get really depressed.

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.040
There are many things in the world

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.000
that you're better off not knowing.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.460
It's because of my job!

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:50.370
I got fat because all I do at work

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:53.440
is sit around being bored, 
eat snacks, and nap!

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.210
What do you mean, bored?

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.680
You need to give the crowd more service!

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.590
I'm stuck in a rut lately.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:05.140
I'm sick of playing on the tire swing 
and sliding down the slide.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.100
It's your job!

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.660
Hey, can I bring a fitness game?

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.610
No.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.970
Could you make a Germanium hot bath?

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.200
Absolutely not.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.380
Let's get an aerobics trainer lady.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:18.370
I said no!

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:24.200
If I only had some kind of motive.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.740
Then I would feel more like dieting.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.900
Well, if you want to go on a diet,

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.840
you can start by actually 
providing service to the crowd.

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.200
Okay, leave it to me!

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.960
I can do it when it matters!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.070
Well then, do it, please.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.280
Wake up, Mr. Panda!

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:02.290
You're so cute, Mr. Panda!

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.330
Service, service!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.520
Service, service!

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.130
He only reacts when 
someone calls him cute.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.490
Service, service!

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.740
His plump body is beyond cute!

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.480
Mr. Panda's overweight.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.770
Panda

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.220
Aim for 130 kilos.
(For now.)

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.910
Become Dream Panda!

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.950
Pa-panda!

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.530
Pa-pan-pan-pa-panda!

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.870
Pa-panda!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.330
Pan-pan-pan-pa-panda!

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:57.120
Diet!

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.760
Diet!

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:06.170
Diet!

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.670
Mr. Panda!

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:19.980
Mr. Panda!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:25.650
Diet, diet! Diet, diet! Diet, diet!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:37.010
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.770
I'm really anxious.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.530
It'll be fine.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:52.510
You've been working 
really hard lately.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:57.010
My goal, for now, is 130 kilograms.

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:18.670
I did it!

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:18.670
You did it!

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:21.190
Congratulations! You achieved your goal!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:27.060
I'm going to work even harder 
to become a trim Dream Panda.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:31.020
Um, you don't have to 
work quite that hard.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.720
I have a present for you since 
you worked so hard, Panda.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:36.850
Ooh, what is it?

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:43.490
I changed it up a little so 
it'll be more fun to slide on.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.630
After all, you said you were in a rut.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.380
Thank you, Mr. Handa!

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:54.200
I was waiting for you.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.920
Let's go down for the 
first time together.

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:57.580
Okay!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:03.680
Yay.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.220
Yay!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.140
Yay!

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.230
What happened?

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.190
Um, well...

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.270
Looks like my tummy got stuck.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:22.460
You're overweight, 
Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.370
I guess I'll have to rebuild it.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.350
Strive for it! Wild Panda.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:53.580
Welcome.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:03.820
Hello.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:08.250
Exactly what are you doing, Panda?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.420
What's with the get up?

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:15.250
I wanted to feel like a bad guy.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.730
It's so cool to be bad!

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.780
Would you like your usual, Panda?

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:23.070
Yes!

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:26.390
Wait, actually, could I get a strong coffee?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.680
What? Strong? 
It's really bitter, though...

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:33.560
I'm feeling bad today.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.110
Here you go, strong coffee.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.790
Thank you for the drink!

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.030
Why not take it off?

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:45.030
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:49.470
So, what made you think 
bad guys were so cool?

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.850
Well, I have trouble making up my mind,

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.830
So I envy really decisive people.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:00.610
I don't think that has anything 
to do with being a bad guy.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.810
Oh, really?

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:06.850
I think I lack a bit of a wild side.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.680
Wild, huh?

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.140
Ack! It's bitter!

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.930
I knew it...

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.560
I'll get you a lighter coffee.

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:23.080
I watched a lot of videos 
to see what being wild is like.

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:24.610
Videos?

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.160
Let's see...

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:38.380
<i>I present to you "candy" the 
color of bright, golden yellow.</i>

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:43.040
<i>Well, aren't you a villain, Echigoya?</i>

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.470
<i>No, no!</i>

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:54.290
I think all of those are 
a little off somehow...

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:58.910
I still can't get the image 
of strong and wild just yet.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.350
Strong and wild, huh?

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.400
Grizzly might be that type.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.900
Ooh, who's that?

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.780
He runs a business. Do you 
want to go there tonight?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:18.640
Is Mr. Grizzly's place 
somewhere around here?

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:21.290
No, it's a little further.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.220
Fukunaga Sports

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.220
Hamanaka Caféteria

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.680
You'll see it right after 
we exit this tunnel.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.990
We're here.

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:18.770
Over here, Panda.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.650
This place is pretty wild.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.670
Somewhat beast-like?

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:32.770
Good evening, Grizzly.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.470
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:38.700
It's been a while.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.980
<i>He really is wild.</i>

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:47.350
As white as ever, you damn polar bear.

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:49.650
Go get a tan at the tanning salon.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.430
No... I don't think that would 
make a difference.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.780
I brought a friend with me today.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.600
N-Nice to meet you.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:06.820
Can't make up your damn mind 
whether you're black or white?

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:11.160
Well, he is a panda.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.660
Well, whatever.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:14.620
Sit.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.630
What'll it be?

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.860
A single malt.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:24.580
Hey, Panda.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.280
Yes?

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:27.370
For you?

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:31.130
Um... a large serving of bamboo...

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:35.010
Sorry, we don't have any 
of that healthy crap.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:40.070
T-Then could I get an iced coffee?

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.640
Don't have any soft drinks either.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:47.940
Then could I get a parfait 
with bamboo leaves...

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.980
I just told you we don't have 
any of that healthy crap here!

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:53.860
Grizzly.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.980
Looks like I don't have a choice.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:59.060
You're a friend of Polar Bear's.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:00.870
I'll get you some coffee.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.760
Any milk?

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:07.870
No, thank you.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:10.840
Actually, yes, please...

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.990
Actually, no thank—

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:15.180
Black or not?!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:19.250
Jeez, short-tempered as ever.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.590
Well, if a panda could decide
 between black or white,

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:25.140
a polar bear would be just a regular bear.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:30.980
Mr. Grizzly is really scary.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.140
You think so?

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.280
Hey, bro.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:42.120
You're so plump and round, 
and you look delicious.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:46.290
I wonder how I should eat you.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:47.690
Maybe I'll just swallow 
you whole <i>(marunomi)</i>.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.090
Perhaps a coconut <i>(yashinomi)</i>.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.800
Maybe I'll barbecue you <i>(baabekyuu)</i>.

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.590
Perhaps miso cucumbers <i>(morokyuu)</i>. {I think they're actually made with like miso or some 
kind of fermented soy sauce... I thought pickled sounded easier but maybe "cucumbers with miso"}{Z: Changed this a bit. If you don't like change feel free to change back.}

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:57.130
Maybe I'll slice you up 
into sashimi <i>(ikezukuri)</i>. {he means when you get sashimi and it's presented to you 
with the head and tail as decoration... I didn't know how else to word that without it being too wordy ^^;;}

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.350
Perhaps trying to look 
younger <i>(wakazukuri)</i>.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:06.770
Hey, you!

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:11.130
Don't be scaring the other 
customers too much.

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.800
I-I'll be going now!

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.010
Hey, Panda.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:27.670
Sorry about that.  
Here you go, coffee.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:33.670
Thank you, Mr. Grizzly!

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:42.720
Hey, Mr. Grizzly.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:43.510
What?

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:47.520
That's you in that picture, right?

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:50.800
Oh, that.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.590
That's when I drove across 
America on my baby.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.290
That's so cool!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.210
It was great.

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:02.450
We rode onward toward the horizon.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:05.910
Wow, that's so cool!

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:11.880
You guys probably enjoy having a 
slow life with no excitement.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.490
I prefer LOHAS.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.490
(Lifestyles of Health and Sustainability)

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:16.330
Doesn't matter what you call it.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.640
The slow life's not that different.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.850
You always did march to the 
beat of your own drum.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:26.070
You only live once.

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.850
You have to go all out.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:31.800
You're so cool, Mr. Grizzly!

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:34.780
I really admire that.

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:36.610
Well, you seem to understand things even

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.790
though you're a friend of Polar Bear.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.110
Hurry up and drink it, it'll get cold.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:48.800
How is it?

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.040
I made an Irish coffee.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:55.690
Well, I may have put in more 
whiskey than coffee, though.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.960
What? That's not...

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.970
Vroom, vroom...

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:22.360
You should bring him again.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:25.450
I won't use instant coffee next time.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.800
Yeah, make it mild next time.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:40.560
Huh?

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.700
Are you awake?

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.040
You carried me out, Polar Bear?

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.040
Yep.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.020
Thanks.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.980
No problem at all.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:56.030
Also, thank you again.

00:20:57.530 --> 00:21:01.930
I think I have a better 
idea of wild now.

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:04.610
That's good. I'm glad I could help.

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:49.890
What do you think, Polar Bear?

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:50.910
Is this wild?

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:54.120
No, I think it's more mild.

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:56.230
See ya.

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:00.500
Oh?

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.550
Where are you going, Panda?

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:11.010
Bad guys never look back.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:13.580
Oh, I see.

00:23:55.010 --> 00:24:04.360
Please Do Not Feed!

00:23:55.010 --> 00:24:24.560
Next Time

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:01.180
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:01.180 --> 00:24:02.960
What's wrong, Panda?

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:07.290
Why doesn't anyone like you, Mr. Penguin?

